    </p>
    <p>
      By taking batched weights as inputs, the system computes the total absolute volumetric yield, fresh wet density, and normalized material requirements per $m^3$. Using Abrams' water-binder relationship modified for supplementary cementitious materials (IS 10262:2019 principles), it projects the 28-day target mean strength ($f'_{ck}$) and characteristic strength ($f_{ck}$), as well as estimated slump.
    </p>

    <h3>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h3>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>How is the characteristic strength (fck) estimated in reverse mode?</h4>
      <p>The estimated 28-day target mean strength ($f'_{ck}$) is computed using an empirical W/B curve relationship ($f'_{ck} \approx 20 + 10 / (W/B)^{1.5}$ with SCM efficiency factors). Characteristic strength is derived by subtracting standard deviation margins ($f_{ck} = f'_{ck} - 1.65 \times S$).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h4>How is workability (slump/flow) derived from batched inputs?</h4>
      <p>Slump estimation analyzes total available water, binder content, and PCE admixture dosage percentage relative to binder mass to forecast workability in millimeters.</p>
    </div>
